---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About — template-test" description="Learn more about the person behind this blog.">
  <header class="mb-12">
    <h1 class="mb-4">About</h1>
    <div class="accent-line"></div>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Welcome. This is a space where I write about the things that occupy my mind —
      technology, artificial intelligence, health, and the quieter moments of personal life.
    </p>

    <p>
      I believe in simplicity. In building things with care. In taking the time to
      understand before rushing to create. This blog is an extension of that philosophy.
    </p>

    <h2>What I Write About</h2>

    <p>
      <strong class="text-burnt-500">Tech</strong> — Tools, workflows, and the craft of building software.
      I'm drawn to minimal setups and thoughtful engineering.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong class="text-burnt-500">AI</strong> — The rapidly shifting landscape of artificial intelligence.
      What it means, where it's going, and how to work alongside it.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong class="text-burnt-500">Personal</strong> — Reflections on life, growth, and the pursuit
      of intentional living in a world that moves too fast.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong class="text-burnt-500">Health</strong> — Physical and mental well-being. Routines,
      habits, and lessons learned through trial and error.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm">
      This site is built with Astro, styled with Tailwind CSS, and designed with
      the principle of Japanese minimalism — where empty space is just as important
      as the content itself.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
